# Files that carry Arabic on purpose, each with the reason on its line.
#
# The rule is that Arabic lives in the translation files and nowhere else. This
# repository IS the translation, so three things in it are Arabic by their nature and
# would be wrong in English. Anything not named here is still held to the rule.

# The glossary of the terms this translation uses, and the arguments for choosing each
# one over the alternatives. Its whole subject is which Arabic word to use; writing it
# in English would leave nothing to read.
GLOSSARY.md

# The summary for Arabic readers, at the end of an otherwise English README. Somebody
# looking for an Arabic translation of OPNsense should be able to tell, in Arabic, that
# this is one.
README.md

# One line: $locales['ar_SA'] = the language name in its own script. A language's name is written in that
# language - OPNsense's own list says Deutsch and Francais, not German and French - so
# this string cannot be in English and cannot be translated, because it is the entry a
# translation would be selected by.
install.sh
